invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_table.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: one limb of one entry of the table of multiples of G is off by
  one: the X coordinate of 3 * 2^102 * G, entry [17][1]. The base
  multiplication reads it for one digit of one window, so a random scalar
  is wrong one time in 32 and no fixed vector need notice.
  bin/p256_equiv_test recomputes every entry from G with p256_point_add
  and p256_point_affine and compares each coordinate byte for byte.

